sis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SSC-AS", "descr": "AS-Social Sciences", "descrformal": "AS-Social Sciences", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPI", "gradingBasisShort": "Opt NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "PSYCH", "catalogNbr": "1131", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "3W2", "sessionBeginDt": "06/22/2026", "sessionEndDt": "07/10/2026", "sessionLong": "Three Week - Second", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Introduction to Human Development provides a broad and foundational overview of field of human development, starting from conception and ending through process of death and dying. The course will start with an outline and explanation of the lifespan perspective in human development. The biological beginnings of life and prenatal development will serve as the start of the discussion of human development, followed by an exploration of physical, cognitive, and socioemotional development at each subsequent stage within the lifespan (e.g., infancy, early childhood, middle & late childhood, etc.). Discussion of each developmental stage will highlight major research findings and their real-world application.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "HD 1130, HD 1150, HD 1170, PSYCH 1131", "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": ["Develop a broad but strong base of knowledge surrounding the field of human development and how human development research is conducted.", "Be able to read and understand, critically think about current research in the field of human development and how research can be applied to the real world.", "Gain an understanding about the different developmental stages and what kind of change is occurring across the domains of physical, cognitive, and socioemotional development.", "Consider your beliefs about development before the course and reconsider the beliefs that are not supported by research.", "Find this class fun and interesting, taking what you learned from the course and be able to apply it in your daily life."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2025FA, 2025SU, 2024FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 373729, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HD", "catalogNbr": "2170", "titleShort": "Adolesc and Emerging Adulthood", "titleLong": "Adolescence and Emerging Adulthood", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-AG", "descr": "AG-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-HE", "descr": "HE-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "HE-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(SBA-AG), (SBA-HE)"}], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "002", "classNbr": 1688, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:30AM", "timeEnd": "12:00PM", "startDt": "07/13/2026", "endDt": "07/31/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "dnt32", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "Nicholas", "lastName": "Tompkins"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit: https://sce.cornell.edu/."}, {"classNotesSeq": 2, "descrlong": "Enrollment open to: Precollege Studies Residential program students. See https://sce.cornell.edu/precollege/residential for more information."}, {"classNotesSeq": 3, "descrlong": "Enrollment open to: Precollege Studies Commuter program students. See https://sce.cornell.edu/precollege/program/on-campus for additional information."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "07/13/2026", "endDt": "07/31/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0009", "crseAttrValue": "PCCOM", "descr": "Precollege Commuter", "descrformal": "Precollege Studies Commuter Program", "attrDescr": "School of Continuing Education", "attrDescrShort": "SCE"}, {"crseAttr": "0009", "crseAttrValue": "PCRES", "descr": "Precollege Residential", "descrformal": "Precollege Studies Residential Progam", "attrDescr": "School of Continuing Education", "attrDescrShort": "SCE"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-AG", "descr": "AG-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-HE", "descr": "HE-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "HE-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPI", "gradingBasisShort": "Opt NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "3W3", "sessionBeginDt": "07/13/2026", "sessionEndDt": "07/31/2026", "sessionLong": "Three Week - Three", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "HD 2170 introduces students to the major theoretical perspectives, research findings, research methods, applications, and controversies in the study of human development during the period of adolescence and the transition to emerging adulthood. The main focus is on individual development, but we view this development from an interdisciplinary perspective. The emphasis in the course is on psychological development, but we also will draw on related fields, such as sociology, anthropology, biology, neuroscience, and education. Within psychology, we will be looking at adolescence and emerging adulthood from the standpoints of developmental, cognitive, social, personality, clinical, and biological psychology. There will be some use of statistics in the course, but sophisticated knowledge of statistics is not required. This is a second-level course, so the emphasis is on creative, analytical, practical, and wise understanding and application of concepts of development.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "HD 1130 or PSYCH 1101.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": ["Understand the theories and research which describe the fundamental changes of adolescence, including social/personality, emotional, biological, and cognitive transitions.", "Comprehend and apply theoretical perspectives and research findings regarding the issues in psychosocial development which come to the forefront in adolescence and emerging adulthood, such as identity, autonomy, intimacy, sexuality and achievement, as well as psychosocial problems.", "Understand theories and research findings that examine the major contexts in which development in adolescence occurs, including families, peers, schools, work, and leisure/mass media.", "Apply what they have learned in this course to their own psychological development, past and present.", "Think creatively, analytically, practically, and wisely about adolescence and the transitions that occur during this period."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2026SP, 2025SU, 2025SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 351490, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "HD", "catalogNbr": "2230", "titleShort": "Intro to Behavioral Neuroscien", "titleLong": "Intro to Behavioral Neuroscience", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "OPHLS-AG", "descr": "AG-Other Physcl & Life Sci Req", "descrformal": "AG-Other Physical and Life Sciences Requirement", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "BIO-AS", "descr": "AS-Biological Sciences", "descrformal": "AS-Biological Sciences", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SCT-IL", "descr": "IL-Science & Technology", "descrformal": "IL-Science and Technology", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [